From fd60a439fe8f0ff838ca8b2eb6125bdee1e88e41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 11:40:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add shared component library, migrate Dompet/Arus Kas +
 others to it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Component standards doc introduced a set of shared widgets that didn't
exist anywhere in the codebase yet. Built them from scratch and
migrated existing screens — including Dompet and Arus Kas from the
previous patch — to use them instead of ad hoc inline styling, per
"gw mau app gw seragam, gak ngasal di komponen2nya".

New shared widgets (lib/core/widgets/):
- app_button.dart — AppButton.primary/secondary/danger
- app_card_shell.dart — AppCardShell (the standard card skin)
- app_text_field.dart — AppTextField.search/form
- app_icon_button.dart — AppIconButton.standard/stepper
- app_empty_state.dart — AppEmptyState
- app_status_badge.dart — AppStatusBadge
- app_item_thumbnail.dart — AppItemThumbnail (photo or deterministic
  initials avatar)
- app_pin_keypad.dart — AppPinKeypad + AppPinDots, extracted from the
  existing PIN login screen (already matched the spec) rather than
  reimplemented; pin_login_screen.dart now uses it
- app_dropdown_title.dart — AppDropdownTitle<T>, the tappable
  dropdown-chevron title IosPageHeader's own doc comment already
  anticipated ("callers needing a tappable title with a dropdown
  chevron... can still center it the same way")
- date_filter_tabs.dart — DateFilterTabs<T>, generalized from
  Riwayat's existing chip-row filter (the proven implementation, not a
  new one) so Arus Kas could reuse it instead of its own private copy
- sliding_pill_tabs.dart — moved from hpp_opname's own widgets folder,
  since it was already the correct, working implementation and had two
  real call sites there

Consolidated three duplicate header widgets found along the way
(ArusKasHeader from the last patch, MenuManagementHeader, and
HppOpnameHeader) — all three independently reimplemented the same
Overlay-based dropdown-title header from scratch, which is exactly
what AppSheetHeader's doc comment warns against for modals and what
IosPageHeader was already set up to support for full-page screens.
All three screens now build AppDropdownTitle and pass it as
IosPageHeader's title, and the three duplicate files are gone.

Also standardized on the app's existing IosPageHeader placement
convention (embedded as the first Column child inside body: SafeArea,
not Scaffold.appBar) — Dompet, Dompet Closing, Arus Kas, and HPP
Opname now match the other five screens using IosPageHeader instead of
introducing a second pattern.

Added dialogTheme to app_theme.dart per the standards doc §16 (radius
20, title/content text style) so AlertDialog usages across the app
share one definition instead of repeating style inline; cleaned up one
redundant inline content style left over from before the theme
existed.

Refactored to use the new widgets: dompet_screen.dart,
dompet_closing_screen.dart, arus_kas_screen.dart,
add_arus_kas_modal.dart, courier_outstanding_card.dart (also swapped
its inline TextField/InputDecoration for AppTextField.form, and its
two color-coded OutlinedButtons for AppButton.secondary + icon, since
the standards doc's button variants are a closed set and courier
resolution isn't a case it names).

Dashboard pull-to-refresh: already implemented (InlineRefreshIndicator
+ custom drag detection, wired to the provider) — not touched this
pass. Reported as not working in the Android emulator but untested on
a real device yet; likely an emulator drag-simulation quirk rather
than a real bug, but worth confirming on-device before assuming it's
fine.

Verified manually (brace/paren balance, every constructor call against
its actual signature, Flutter-version-safe API choices) since this
environment has no Flutter SDK to run flutter analyze — please run it
before merging.
